ry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="t102" value="[nothing found]" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="712" y="1088" width="170" height="16" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="b103" value="Show the unavailable message" style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="490" y="1447" width="190" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="e104" value="" style="html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#000000;endArrow=open;endSize=10;exitX=0.0000;exitY=0.5000;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1.0000;entryY=0.5000;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="b69" target="b103"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="b105" value="" style="ellipse;shape=endState;fillColor=#000000;strokeColor=#000000;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="574" y="1506" width="22" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="e106" value="" style="html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#000000;endArrow=open;endSize=10;exitX=0.5000;exitY=1.0000;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5000;entryY=0.0000;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="b103" target="b105"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="t107" value="[no response in time]" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="712" y="1448" width="170" height="16" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="b108" value="&lt;b&gt;How to read&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Rounded shapes with a verb: actions. Diamond with several arrows out: decision, each arrow has a guard in [ ]; diamond with several arrows in: merge. Thick bar: fork (one flow becomes parallel flows) or join (parallel flows wait for each other). Dot: start; dot in a ring: end. Rectangles with underlined names: objects that the actions create or use.&lt;br&gt;The flow goes from top to bottom. The preparing message (left) runs in parallel with the checks (step 7 of UC-04), then the flows join. Each exception ends the whole activity, as in the scenario of UC-04." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="930" y="1960" width="860" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="b109" value="&lt;b&gt;Mapping to the class diagram&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Check access → AiAssistant.checkAccess; Check the daily limit → isLimitReached (AiUsageRecord.countToday); Check whether the task is graded → isAboutGradedTask; Find relevant slides → MaterialIndex.findRelevant; Remove personal data → removePersonalData; Send the question → ILlmClient.generate; Show … → LecturePage.showMessage / showResult." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1960" width="860" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>